-- pending: refused #491
-- now: 14:1: `count` loops, so it is called in direct style one step at a time, and a borrow at `'a` cannot stay open across its steps: it may take one borrow of a cell at `'a`, `imm 'a A` or `mut 'a A`, which it borrows again at each step (SPEC §14, borrow scopes over loops; decision 71). Pass the other borrowed values as owned copies, or iterate by index with a counted `for`
--
-- A counted `for` over a view bound in the body of a function with a lifetime parameter. The
-- loop is total, bounded by the view's length (SPEC §16), as the same loop over the parameter
-- itself is; the view is not among the parameters the elaboration types before deciding whether
-- the body loops (`lentDef`), so its source has no type and the function is taken to loop. A
-- view parameter followed by a pair parameter (`buf A`) is refused the same way.
--
-- Once it lands: `i32[3]`, `live 0`.

include slice

fn count<'a>(v: array_imm 'a u8) -> i32 =
  let (v, w) = array_copy['a, u8] v;
  let mut k = 0;
  for x in w { k = k + 1 };
  k

main -> i32 =
  let a = array_new[u8] (3, !{ i -> to_u8(i) });
  let n = count(&a);
  n
